==============================================================================
INTERPRETATION RULES
==============================================================================
1. ISIMIP3a histsoc land use is a historical reconstruction, not direct annual observation.
2. Sen slope and Mann-Kendall quantify monotonic historical tendencies; they do not establish causality.
3. OLS is reported for comparability, but reconstructed annual values are temporally autocorrelated, so OLS p-values should not be treated as fully independent-year evidence.
4. Breakpoints are exploratory structural descriptors. Do not label them as known historical events without independent documentary evidence.
5. 70 km is the primary scale; 25 and 50 km are spatial sensitivity analyses.
6. Percentages refer to the entire circular coastal buffer, including marine area, not terrestrial land alone.

